# Shared by both hypridle configs (hypridle.conf, hypridle-nolock.conf) so the
# two modes cannot drift apart on the safety-critical settings.
#
# before_sleep_cmd is why presentation mode holds a systemd idle inhibitor
# rather than stopping the daemon: an inhibitor pauses the listeners while
# leaving these armed, so closing the lid still locks. Killing hypridle
# disarmed lock-on-suspend entirely.
#
# 🚨 inhibit_sleep = 3 is what makes lock-before-suspend RELIABLE, and no script
# can substitute for it. hypridle SPAWNS before_sleep_cmd and releases the
# logind delay inhibitor in the same instant -- measured 2026-09-12:
#   Executing .../lock-before-sleep / Process Created with pid 13271
#   Releasing the sleep inhibitor!
# both at 13:11:18 -- so a before_sleep_cmd that waits for the lock is waiting
# after the inhibitor is already gone. Mode 3 instead holds the inhibitor until
# the compositor reports the session LOCKED (Hypridle.cpp: onLocked() calls
# uninhibitSleep(), onUnlocked() calls inhibitSleep()), which is the same fact a
# script could only poll for, held by the thing that owns the inhibitor.
general {
    lock_cmd = ~/.local/lib/scripts/desktop/immediate-lock  # Single lock entry point (re-entrancy guarded)
    before_sleep_cmd = loginctl lock-session                # Lock before suspend
    inhibit_sleep = 3                                      # Hold sleep until LOCKED, not until spawned
    # Display back on, then (laptop only) re-enumerate audio. Every resume leaks one orphaned
    # PipeWire sink node (its device.id points at a device that no longer
    # exists); after 17 suspends this laptop had 18 nodes all named
    # alsa_output.pci-0000_00_1f.3.analog-stereo. Quickshell resolves the
    # default sink BY NAME (defaults.cpp findNodeByName), so it binds whichever
    # duplicate comes first and the OSD then tracks a node nothing ever changes
    # — volume keys look dead while pamixer is in fact moving the real sink.
    # Restarting wireplumber destroys its objects and rebuilds a clean registry.
    # Measured on the laptop only; on the desktop a restart would just cut any
    # stream playing across the suspend.
    after_sleep_cmd = hyprctl dispatch 'hl.dsp.dpms({ action = "on" })'{{ if eq .chassisType "laptop" }}; systemctl --user restart wireplumber{{ end }}

    # True session lock/unlock events. Unlike a listener's on-resume (which fires
    # the instant the mouse moves, BEFORE authentication), on_unlock_cmd only
    # fires once the user has actually authenticated.
    # ⚠️ inhibit_sleep = 3 does NOT disable these, despite how hypridle's own
    # warning reads. That warning is guarded by `if (!m_sWaylandState.lockNotifier)`
    # and is about a compositor MISSING hyprland-lock-notify-v1. Hyprland has it,
    # and the journal proves it: "Wayland session got locked" is the event that
    # fires them, and onLocked() spawns on_lock_cmd whatever the inhibit mode is.
    on_lock_cmd = ~/.local/lib/scripts/core/hook-runner lock-change lock
    on_unlock_cmd = ~/.local/lib/scripts/core/hook-runner lock-change unlock
}
